# Workspace Branding

Configure your workspace's default branding settings. These settings apply across your dashboard and serve as defaults for all events.

## Accessing Branding Settings

To configure workspace branding:

1. Click **Settings** in the sidebar
2. Select **Branding** from the settings menu

## Logo Upload

### Light Mode Logo

Your primary logo displayed on light backgrounds:

1. Click the upload area under "Logo (Light Mode)"
2. Select an image file from your computer
3. The logo appears in the preview

**Recommendations:**

- Format: PNG or SVG for best quality
- Background: Transparent preferred
- Size: At least 200px wide for crisp display
- File size: Under 500KB for fast loading

### Dark Mode Logo (Optional)

A separate logo optimized for dark backgrounds:

1. Click the upload area under "Logo (Dark Mode)"
2. Select an image file
3. This logo is used when dark mode is active

{% callout type="info" %}
If you don't upload a dark mode logo, the light mode logo will be used everywhere. Consider uploading a dark mode version if your logo doesn't look good on dark backgrounds.
{% /callout %}

## Color Settings

### Primary Color

Your main brand color, used for:

- Action buttons (Submit, Save, Confirm)
- Active navigation indicators
- Key highlights and accents

To set the primary color:

1. Click the color picker under "Primary Color"
2. Choose from preset colors or enter a custom hex code
3. The preview updates to show your selection

### Accent Color

A secondary color for supporting elements:

- Links and hyperlinks
- Secondary buttons
- Decorative accents

Set it the same way as the primary color.

## Dark Mode Colors (Optional)

For optimal appearance in dark mode, you can specify different color values:

### Primary Color (Dark)

A lighter or adjusted version of your primary color that looks better on dark backgrounds.

### Accent Color (Dark)

An adjusted accent color for dark mode.

{% callout type="info" %}
If you don't set dark mode colors, the light mode colors are used. Most colors work well in both modes, but some benefit from adjustment.
{% /callout %}

## Card Accent Settings

Add a colored accent bar to cards throughout the dashboard:

### Enable Card Accent

Toggle the **Enable Card Accent** switch to add accent bars to cards.

### Accent Color

Choose the color for the accent bar. By default, this uses your primary color, but you can select any color.

### Position

Choose where the accent bar appears on cards:

- **Top** - Accent bar at the top edge
- **Bottom** - Accent bar at the bottom edge
- **Left** - Accent bar on the left side
- **Right** - Accent bar on the right side

### Thickness

Select the thickness of the accent bar:

- **Thin** - Subtle accent line
- **Medium** - Standard accent bar
- **Thick** - Bold accent bar

## Section Header Settings

Customize how section headers appear:

### Background Color

Set a background color for section headers. Leave empty to use the default transparent background.

### Text Color

Set the text color for section headers. Leave empty to use the default text color.

{% callout type="info" %}
Section header styling affects headers throughout the dashboard, giving your workspace a cohesive branded appearance.
{% /callout %}

## Live Preview

The preview panel on the right shows how your branding will look:

- **Logo display** - See your logo as it will appear
- **Button styling** - Primary button with your color
- **Link styling** - Accent color on links
- **Card accent** - Preview of card accent styling
- **Toggle theme** - Switch between light and dark mode preview

Use the sun/moon icon to toggle the preview between light and dark mode.

## Saving Changes

Click **Save Changes** to apply your branding settings. Changes take effect immediately:

- Dashboard updates with new colors
- New events inherit these settings
- Existing events using inheritance are updated

## Best Practices

### Choose Accessible Colors

Ensure sufficient contrast between:

- Button colors and white text
- Link colors and background
- Logo and its background

### Test Both Modes

Always preview your branding in both light and dark mode to ensure it looks good in both contexts.

### Use Consistent Branding

Match your workspace branding to your organization's brand guidelines for a professional, cohesive appearance.
